From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcp: Implement the iostream move constructors, move assignments and basic_ios::move.

The move members of the iostream classes were spec stubs in msvcp100 and
later: the move constructors and move assignments of basic_istream,
basic_ostream and basic_iostream and basic_ios::move (rvalue, and from
msvcp110 also lvalue), for char, wchar_t and unsigned short. As the C++
standard words them: the new stream default-constructs its basic_ios and
takes the source's state, tie (and gcount) but no stream buffer; the
source keeps its stream buffer and loses its tie; move assignment swaps.
msvcp120_app and msvcp_win forward.
---
